<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <RootNamespace>Harness.Run</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>harness-run</AssemblyName>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    THE LAST LINK: spec -> map -> IR -> deploy -> run -> results.

    Harness.Loop was a library with no entry point - it could be unit-tested and could not be RUN, so
    the loop existed and nothing could invoke it. This is the composition root.

    IT OWNS NO DEVICE POLICY OF ITS OWN. The fence is DeviceGuard's, consulted before any socket; the
    only gateways reachable from here are the VERIFYING one (reads the build stamp, refuses any
    mismatch, changes nothing) and the REFUSING one. *** THERE IS NO FLAG THAT ASSERTS A DEPLOYMENT
    INSTEAD OF MEASURING ONE *** - a gateway reporting Loaded without loading is one edit from a
    gateway that lies, and that edit must not be available in a binary an operator runs.

    Every decision lives in LoopCli, which takes its transport as a FACTORY, so the whole CLI is
    exercised in tests without a process and without a socket.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Harness.Gate\Harness.Gate.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Harness.Loop\Harness.Loop.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Harness.Wire\Harness.Wire.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\device-guard\DeviceGuard\DeviceGuard.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
